> Tesco sell fresh yeast in multiples of 100 g.

Put the  @strong white flour{500%g} and @caster sugar{100%g} in a large bowl. Add the @fresh yeast{28%g}(or 10 g dried yeast) on one side of the bowl and the @salt{10%g} on the other. Add the @unsalted butter{150%g}(softened) and 200ml of the @whole milk{250%ml} and stir together.

Add the remaining milk and bring the mixture together to form a soft dough. Transfer to a generously floured work surface and knead for 6 to ~{7%minutes}, or until smooth and pliable.

Mix the @ground nutmeg{pinch}, @ground cloves{pinch}, @vanilla extract{0.5%tsp}, @almond extract{2%drops}, @almonds, blanched{55%g}(finely chopped), @raisins{200%g}, @currants{100%g}, and @candied peel{125%g} together in a large bowl. Put the dough on top and knead from the outside into the centre incorporating the dried fruit and spices. When everything has been fully incorporated, cover the bowl with cling film and leave to rise for 1 to ~{2%hours} in a warm place, or until doubled in size.

Line a baking tray with parchment.

Flatten the dough and roll out on a lightly floured work surface into a rectangle about 35×45 cm (or so the short side of the dough matches the longest side of the baking tray). Brush with the @unsalted butter{25%g}(melted).

If the @./Sweet/Marzipan{225%g}(preferably soft paste) is soft enough then spread it over the dough, leaving a gap at the bottom and top. Otherwise roll out the marzipan to about 35×15 cm (the long side should approximately match the width of the dough), and then place on top of the dough in the middle.

Roll the dough up to enclose the marzipan and transfer to a baking tray lined with baking parchment. Cover and leave to rise for about ~{1%hour}, or until risen and doubled in size.

When the dough is risen, preheat the oven to 180°C and bake for ~{15%minutes}.

Reduce the heat to 130°C and bake for a further ~{45%minutes}.

= Serve =

Remove from the oven, brush with @unsalted butter{25%g}(melted), and dust with @icing sugar{2%tbsp}. Serve cold.